            <ArticleTitle>The spectrum of 5-fluorouracil cardiotoxicity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiotoxicity is a rare but serious complication of 5-fluorouracil therapy. Coronary vasospasm and, less frequently, acute myocarditis have been identified as underlying mechanisms. We report a case of severe toxicity in a relatively young and fit male patient being treated for metastatic colonic adenocarcinoma displaying characteristics that cannot be explained by either mechanism alone.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
